# 6. MEMBER JOINING AND VERIFICATION SYSTEM

This is a very important feature.

I want two supported ways for someone to join a team.

METHOD A — ADMIN ADDS A MEMBER

1. Admin opens Team Management.
2. Admin selects Add Member.
3. Admin searches for or invites a user using their registered email or secure invitation.
4. The invited user receives an invitation.
5. The user accepts the invitation.
6. Membership is verified.
7. The member appears in the team member list.

METHOD B — VERIFIED MEMBER INVITES ANOTHER MEMBER

1. An existing verified team member can generate a secure invitation.
2. The invitation contains a unique, non-guessable invitation token.
3. The new person signs in using their individual account.
4. The invitation is validated.
5. The new member accepts the invitation.
6. The system verifies the invitation and adds the member to the team.
7. The administrator can see the new member in the team.

A verified member must not be able to assign administrator privileges or override team security policies.

The administrator must be able to disable member-generated invitations.

All invitation tokens must have expiration and single-use protection.

