# 7. VERY IMPORTANT: PERMANENT REMOVAL RESTRICTION

This condition must be implemented strictly.

When the Team Admin removes a member:

1. Remove that member from the active team.
2. Immediately revoke their team access.
3. Immediately revoke their access to the team's active missions.
4. Stop their ability to view team member locations.
5. Stop their ability to upload location updates to that team's mission.
6. Remove them from the live radar.
7. Record the removal in the team audit history.
8. Add their UID to a permanent team-specific blocked membership list.

MOST IMPORTANT RULE:

**Once an administrator removes a member, that person must NEVER be able to rejoin that team through a mission code, invitation link, QR code, another member's invitation, or self-joining process.**

Only the Team Admin can manually reinstate that person.

If the administrator does not reinstate them, the person must remain blocked.

Even another verified member must not be able to invite or add a removed person back.

Implement server-side checks for this rule.

Do not rely only on hiding buttons in the UI.

A removed member must lose access immediately, including access through an already-open application session.

